  "predicted_delta_text": "**Prediction**:  \n- **S11_db improves by ~10 dB** (from -0.69 dB to ~9.3 dB).  \n- Replacing **NM3 (short)** with **PMOS PM1 (diode-connected)** removes the **VDD-VSS short**, and creates a **stable biasing path**.  \n- PMOS in diode mode (gate-drain at n6) **draws current from VDD to n7**, which is **not grounded** \u2192 avoids short.  \n- The **biasing voltage at n6** is now set by **R1/R2** and **PM1**, which is more stable than NMOS.  \n- This enables **proper DC operating point**, allowing **SPICE optimizer to tune input network** and improve **S11**.\n\n---\n\n### Summary of Predictions:\n| Edit | Structural Change | Predicted S11_db Improvement |\n|------|-------------------|-------------------------------|\n| 1    | Fix NM3 (diode PMOS or NMOS) | +12 dB (from -0.69 \u2192 ~11.3 dB) |\n| 2    | Add shunt C3 at input | +8 dB (from -0.69 \u2192 ~7.3 dB) |\n| 3    | Replace NM3 with PMOS | +10 dB (from -0.69 \u2192 ~9.3 dB) |\n\nAll edits **fix the fatal VDD-VSS short** caused by NM3 and **enable a functional LNA** with **potential for good S11**.",
